# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution; 1 rad = 1.59 mm). hv0.sim_dist, zeroed at the failure, is how
# far the axis went.
# The dynamic brake with the DC bus high (above high_dc_volt; here set below
# the bus): rv backs off towards a plain short, so less energy goes into
# the bus, but not past the current target (2 A here): the current comes
# first. Before, the short's transient (~3.4 A) went over 1.3 x the target
# and the brake gave up (coasting, ~10 rad); now it brakes, ~2 rad. If the
# bus still rises the F3 switches off at ABS_MAX_VOLT (bus_regen_f3.test).
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
dbrake0.max_cur = 2
dbrake0.high_dc_volt = 250
hv0.sim_dist = 0
enc_fb0.sim_fail = 1
run 0.0024
@sample dbrake0.rv 0.0004 0.002
@sample hv0.abs_cur 0.0004 0.002
run 0.01
dbrake0.gave_up
fault0.en_out
run 0.4
hv0.sim_dist
@expect max|hv0.abs_cur| < 2.6
@expect dbrake0.gave_up == 0
@expect hv0.sim_dist < 3
